---
name: ai-prompt-optimizer-setup
description: Configure or inspect the local Codex on-demand preference for the installed AI Prompt Optimizer plugin when the user requests setup. Does not install a second skill or update plugin files. Not for ordinary prompt refinement.
---

# Configure AI Prompt Optimizer

Use only for local Codex environments with filesystem and execution tools. If unavailable,
explain that local setup cannot run in this environment; do not claim configuration success.

Locate the sibling `../ai-prompt-optimizer/` skill relative to this skill folder.
Read that skill's `references/installation.md` for the maintained workflow and the actual
command flags. Use its `scripts/manage_install.py`; never write a new installer ad hoc.

Offer one recommended choice: enable on-demand guidance for ambiguous/complex tasks;
the alternative is to keep the host's normal skill selection without adding guidance.
State that enabling guidance writes a bounded preference in the active Codex guidance file.
If the user already requested this setting, proceed under that authorization.

For plugin setup, run `configure --plugin-path <absolute-sibling-skill-path>` with
`--mode on-demand` or `--mode host`, and `--yes` only for an authorized choice.
Do not run `install`: the host already installed the plugin. Resolve duplicate standalone
copies without deleting user edits. The host owns plugin updates and removal.

Report installation/configuration checks separately from actual client discovery. Do not
claim the plugin is registered, auto-onboarded or invoked just because files exist.
